{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a5cb3e05865aef75","name":"Redemption","source":{"id":"source:reference-a5cb3e05865aef75","title":"Redemption","revision":18448,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:08:49Z","sha256":"d74beae062b3b9cdb12f1d21599c1d38cd2a7f6155f8ac1fa441d7e062ddb3ff","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18448","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Redemption&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a5cb3e05865aef75","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"}," is to Redeem a character that has been corrupted or otherwise turned to evil. Many Jedi seek to turn their fallen brethren away from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". A Rebel agent might seek to turn his brother, an Imperial officer, away from the evil Empire, redeeming him back to the side of justice and freedom. The target of this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"}," should be someone who has fallen from the light in some way, whether that means turning to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", or simply siding with evil over good. Turning someone away from their wicked ways is usually very difficult and requires far more than simple persuasion. Often a character that fulfills this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"}," does not survive it, and sometimes neither does their redeemed target. Additionally, you may be your own target for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"},", making your own Redemption the means of fulfilling it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Examples of this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny","referenceId":"reference:373d368333d789ee"}," include Luke Skywalker turning Darth Vader away from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," and Revan's redemption of Bastila Shan on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Star Forge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Star_Forge"},". You might convince one of the new Sith to abandon their dark ways, or inspire an Imperial Knight to join ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},". Or you might convince an Imperial officer to defect to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Destiny Bonus:"]}," You gain a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Destiny Penalty:"]}," You lose one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"},". If you have no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"}," to lose, you take a -1 penalty on attack rolls until you gain a level."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Destiny Fulfilled:"]}," The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"}," of the Redeemed character is reduced to 1, and they lose any remaining ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},". You gain a number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"}," equal to 3 + the number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"}," the Redeemed character lost."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
